1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,240
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:02,560
Lesson 2: Earth Movement.

3
00:00:04,687 --> 00:00:05,947
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:07,647 --> 00:00:09,227
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:09,567 --> 00:00:10,507
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:10,587 --> 00:00:12,047
Understand that the Earth is spherical.

7
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:14,187
Identify the two types of movements of

8
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:14,587
the Earth.

9
00:00:14,967 --> 00:00:16,527
Explain rotation and its effects.

10
00:00:16,927 --> 00:00:18,707
Understand revolution and its effects.

11
00:00:19,107 --> 00:00:21,227
Learn about different seasons caused by revolution.

12
00:00:21,727 --> 00:00:24,007
Define solstices and equinoxes and when they

13
00:00:24,087 --> 00:00:24,407
occur.

14
00:00:26,233 --> 00:00:26,973
Start-Up Activity.

15
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:30,753
Take a ball and spin it.

16
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:32,053
Notice how it moves.

17
00:00:32,613 --> 00:00:34,233
Imagine this is the Earth moving in

18
00:00:34,313 --> 00:00:34,633
space.

19
00:00:35,013 --> 00:00:37,353
The Earth moves in two ways—let's explore

20
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:38,753
these movements and their effects!

21
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:42,280
Who proved that the earth is spherical?

22
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:47,420
Many ancient civilizations believed that the Earth

23
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:48,000
was flat.

24
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,100
However, Greek philosopher Pythagoras was one of

25
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:52,680
the first to suggest that the Earth

26
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:53,200
is spherical.

27
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:56,760
Later, Aristotle provided evidence by observing how

28
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:58,780
ships disappear over the horizon and how

29
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:00,260
the Earth's shadow on the Moon is

30
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:01,700
curved during a lunar eclipse.

31
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:04,800
Ferdinand Magellan's voyage around the world further

32
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:06,300
confirmed that the Earth is round.

33
00:01:07,919 --> 00:01:09,479
The Two Movements of the Earth.

34
00:01:11,459 --> 00:01:13,159
The Earth moves in two ways:

35
00:01:13,579 --> 00:01:15,439
Rotation – The Earth spins on its

36
00:01:15,519 --> 00:01:16,599
axis around itself.

37
00:01:17,079 --> 00:01:18,979
Revolution – The Earth moves around the

38
00:01:19,059 --> 00:01:19,379
Sun.

39
00:01:20,879 --> 00:01:21,279
Rotation.

40
00:01:21,359 --> 00:01:26,099
Rotation is the movement of the Earth

41
00:01:26,179 --> 00:01:28,199
around its own axis is called Rotation.

42
00:01:29,079 --> 00:01:30,899
The earth rotates from west to east.

43
00:01:31,439 --> 00:01:33,419
It completes one full rotation in 24

44
00:01:33,499 --> 00:01:33,819
hours.

45
00:01:34,259 --> 00:01:35,959
The speed of rotation is faster at

46
00:01:36,039 --> 00:01:37,599
the equator and slower at the poles.

47
00:01:38,259 --> 00:01:39,739
The axis is tilted at an angle

48
00:01:39,819 --> 00:01:41,692
of 23.5°.

49
00:01:41,839 --> 00:01:43,559
As the Earth is spherical in shape,

50
00:01:43,799 --> 00:01:45,339
only one half of the Earth receives

51
00:01:45,419 --> 00:01:46,339
sunlight at a time.

52
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:49,259
Thus, the side of the Earth facing

53
00:01:49,339 --> 00:01:50,439
the Sun experience day.

54
00:01:51,059 --> 00:01:51,759
On the other hand,

55
00:01:52,019 --> 00:01:52,559
the other half,

56
00:01:52,859 --> 00:01:53,999
or the part away from the sun,

57
00:01:54,319 --> 00:01:55,299
experiences night.

58
00:01:55,679 --> 00:01:56,619
As the Earth rotates,

59
00:01:56,779 --> 00:01:58,359
the lighted part moves into the darkness.

60
00:01:59,459 --> 00:02:00,999
Rotation causes day and night.

61
00:02:02,939 --> 00:02:03,879
Do You Know?

62
00:02:06,139 --> 00:02:08,239
The Earth rotates at a speed of

63
00:02:08,319 --> 00:02:11,799
1,670 kilometers per hour at the equator,

64
00:02:12,339 --> 00:02:14,173
but we don’t feel it because we’re

65
00:02:14,253 --> 00:02:15,239
moving along with it!

66
00:02:16,827 --> 00:02:17,587
Revolution.

67
00:02:19,887 --> 00:02:21,467
Revolution is the movement of the Earth

68
00:02:21,547 --> 00:02:22,867
around the Sun in a fixed path

69
00:02:22,947 --> 00:02:23,507
called an orbit.

70
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:25,267
The Earth revolves around the Sun in

71
00:02:25,347 --> 00:02:26,027
an elliptical orbit.

72
00:02:26,587 --> 00:02:29,367
It takes 365¼ days (one year) to

73
00:02:29,447 --> 00:02:30,227
complete one revolution.

74
00:02:31,227 --> 00:02:32,447
The tilt of the Earth's axis remains

75
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:33,567
the same during revolution.

76
00:02:34,747 --> 00:02:35,767
Revolution causes seasonal changes.

77
00:02:37,147 --> 00:02:38,187
The revolution of the Earth and the

78
00:02:38,267 --> 00:02:39,567
tilt of its axis cause different seasons:

79
00:02:40,047 --> 00:02:41,467
Summer – The hemisphere tilted towards the

80
00:02:41,547 --> 00:02:42,347
Sun experiences summer.

81
00:02:43,967 --> 00:02:45,647
Winter – The hemisphere tilted away from

82
00:02:45,727 --> 00:02:46,627
the Sun experiences winter.

83
00:02:47,947 --> 00:02:49,227
Spring – Occurs between winter and summer

84
00:02:49,307 --> 00:02:50,487
when the temperature starts rising.

85
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:53,047
Autumn – Occurs between summer and winter

86
00:02:53,127 --> 00:02:54,267
when the temperature starts dropping.

87
00:02:56,583 --> 00:02:57,563
Let's Learn More.

88
00:02:59,943 --> 00:03:01,883
A day on Earth is actually 23

89
00:03:01,963 --> 00:03:03,423
hours, 56 minutes,

90
00:03:03,863 --> 00:03:05,583
not exactly 24 hours,

91
00:03:05,943 --> 00:03:07,563
but we round it off to 24

92
00:03:07,643 --> 00:03:09,363
hours because it’s easier to keep track

93
00:03:09,443 --> 00:03:09,783
of time.

94
00:03:11,486 --> 00:03:13,686
What is Solstice and When Does It

95
00:03:13,766 --> 00:03:14,086
Occur?

96
00:03:16,466 --> 00:03:17,726
A solstice is a day,

97
00:03:18,066 --> 00:03:20,026
when the sun shines vertically over a

98
00:03:20,106 --> 00:03:22,366
Tropic (both cancer and Capricorn) in the

99
00:03:22,446 --> 00:03:24,146
afternoon and the day is the longest

100
00:03:24,226 --> 00:03:25,146
in that hemisphere.

101
00:03:25,906 --> 00:03:27,146
On 22 December,

102
00:03:27,546 --> 00:03:29,066
the rays of the sun fall directly

103
00:03:29,146 --> 00:03:30,626
over the Tropic of Capricorn.

104
00:03:31,086 --> 00:03:32,506
This is the longest day in Southern

105
00:03:32,586 --> 00:03:34,166
Hemisphere (summer season),

106
00:03:34,606 --> 00:03:35,866
while in the Northern Hemisphere,

107
00:03:36,266 --> 00:03:38,366
it is the shortest day (winter season).

108
00:03:38,926 --> 00:03:40,406
This is called 'Winter Solstice.

109
00:03:40,486 --> 00:03:41,866
On 21 June,

110
00:03:42,306 --> 00:03:44,226
sunlight falls vertically over the Tropic of

111
00:03:44,306 --> 00:03:44,626
Cancer.

112
00:03:45,166 --> 00:03:46,526
This is the longest day in Northern

113
00:03:46,606 --> 00:03:48,869
Hemisphere and hence it is called 'Summer

114
00:03:48,949 --> 00:03:50,586
Solstice', while in the Southern Hemisphere,

115
00:03:51,006 --> 00:03:52,006
it is the shortest day.

116
00:03:53,588 --> 00:03:54,768
Let's Learn More.

117
00:03:57,148 --> 00:03:59,228
Earth keeps rotating due to inertia,

118
00:03:59,688 --> 00:04:01,948
the same reason you continue moving forward

119
00:04:02,028 --> 00:04:03,548
when you stop a bike suddenly.

120
00:04:04,088 --> 00:04:06,288
This movement doesn’t stop because there’s no

121
00:04:06,368 --> 00:04:08,208
friction in space to slow it down!

122
00:04:09,838 --> 00:04:11,618
What is Equinox and When Does It

123
00:04:11,698 --> 00:04:12,018
Occur?

124
00:04:14,458 --> 00:04:16,438
The sun falls directly on the equator

125
00:04:16,518 --> 00:04:17,578
two times in a year.

126
00:04:18,058 --> 00:04:19,918
During this period there is equal length

127
00:04:19,998 --> 00:04:21,318
of day and night all over the

128
00:04:21,398 --> 00:04:21,718
world.

129
00:04:22,118 --> 00:04:23,018
In Northern Hemisphere,

130
00:04:23,518 --> 00:04:25,158
the March Equinox is called the Vernal

131
00:04:25,238 --> 00:04:27,698
or Spring Equinox while September Equinox is

132
00:04:27,778 --> 00:04:29,098
called Autumnal Equinox.

133
00:04:29,718 --> 00:04:32,018
Spring Equinox (March 21st) marks the beginning

134
00:04:32,098 --> 00:04:32,458
of spring.

135
00:04:32,538 --> 00:04:35,578
Autumn Equinox (September 23rd) marks the beginning

136
00:04:35,658 --> 00:04:36,138
of autumn.

137
00:04:37,847 --> 00:04:38,427
Recall.

138
00:04:41,227 --> 00:04:41,887
The Earth's movements,

139
00:04:42,167 --> 00:04:43,107
rotation and revolution,

140
00:04:43,487 --> 00:04:44,927
have significant affects on our lives.

141
00:04:45,567 --> 00:04:46,907
Rotation causes day and night,

142
00:04:47,067 --> 00:04:48,487
while revolution leads to the change of

143
00:04:48,567 --> 00:04:48,887
seasons.

144
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:51,347
Solstices and equinoxes mark the shift in

145
00:04:51,427 --> 00:04:53,147
seasons, playing an essential role in our

146
00:04:53,227 --> 00:04:54,067
climate and timekeeping.

147
00:04:55,782 --> 00:04:56,462
Let's Remember.

148
00:04:56,742 --> 00:05:00,062
The Earth moves in two ways:

149
00:05:00,682 --> 00:05:01,422
rotation and revolution.

150
00:05:02,022 --> 00:05:03,222
Rotation causes day and night,

151
00:05:03,422 --> 00:05:04,702
while revolution causes seasons.

152
00:05:05,222 --> 00:05:06,882
The Earth completes one rotation in 24

153
00:05:06,962 --> 00:05:09,802
hours and one revolution in 365¼ days.

154
00:05:10,542 --> 00:05:12,062
Solstices occur in June and December,

155
00:05:12,402 --> 00:05:13,862
marking the longest and shortest days.

156
00:05:14,462 --> 00:05:15,822
Equinoxes occur in March and September,

157
00:05:16,062 --> 00:05:17,082
when day and night are equal.

158
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:19,400
Word Bank.

159
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,460
Rotation – Spinning of the Earth on

160
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:24,060
its axis.

161
00:05:24,540 --> 00:05:26,340
Revolution – Movement of the Earth around

162
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:26,760
the Sun.

163
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:28,960
Orbit – The path of the Earth

164
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:29,760
around the Sun.

165
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:31,860
Solstice – When the Sun is at

166
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:33,580
its farthest point north or south.

167
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:35,700
Equinox – When day and night are

168
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:36,100
equal.
